            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2484/rcr.v7i3.524</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 33-year-old male with known thalassemia intermedia presented with acute mid-back pain. Radiography and MRI were useful to evaluate the extent of iron deposition and assess for complications (such as cirrhosis) of the disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
